silvio berlusconi was not in court to  hear the verdict the ruling by the Milan  Court has no immediate impact on the  former prime minister because as a  member of the Senate he enjoys  parliamentary immunity but the Senate is  expected to vote next month on whether  to expel him if it does the ban would  take effect Berlusconi would be  prohibited from taking part in any  elections either as a candidate or as a  voter the decision stems from a Supreme  Court ruling on August the first which  upheld a conviction for tax fraud  against Berlusconi linked to his firm  mediaset if the Senate expels Berlusconi  he will also have to serve a one-year  sentence he has opted to do community  service rather than be under house  arrest but Berlusconi still has some  public support we must remember that he  employed so many people I can't think of  any other politician who did anything  concrete like that in his life  immediately after the court ruling  Berlusconi's lawyer said he would appeal  against the ban from political office
 

